<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04ZK">Construction <span data-tag="04ZK">1.1.2.1</span> <span class="named">(Degeneracy Operators)</span>.</a> For every pair of integers $0 \leq i \leq n$ we let $\sigma ^{i}_{n}: [n+1] \twoheadrightarrow [n]$ denote the nondecreasing function given by the formula </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \sigma ^{i}_{n}( j) = \begin{cases}  j &amp;  \text{ if } j \leq i \\  j-1 &amp;  \text{ if } j &gt; i. \end{cases} \]
</div>
<p> If $C_{\bullet }$ is a simplicial object of a category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, then we can evaluate $C_{\bullet }$ on the morphism $\sigma ^{i}_{n}$ to obtain a morphism from $C_{n}$ to $C_{n+1}$. We will denote this map by $s^{n}_{i}: C_{n} \rightarrow C_{n+1}$ and refer to it as the <em>$i$th degeneracy operator</em>. </p>
</article>
